title: Variant coverage — inventory empty (engine lottery)
story: familyzoo
description: Verify that stdlib's empty-inventory message picker keeps choosing among the four variants we expect. Re-runs over CI exercise the picker stochastically.

---

# This is a Layer B variant-coverage scenario (see CLAUDE.md → Testing).
#
# stdlib's inventory action picks one of FOUR message IDs at random when
# the player is empty. From node_modules/@sharpee/stdlib/actions/standard/
# inventory/inventory.js:104:
#
#   const emptyMessages = ['inventory_empty', 'nothing_at_all',
#                          'hands_empty', 'pockets_empty'];
#   messageId = emptyMessages[Math.floor(Math.random() * emptyMessages.length)];
#
# Rendered (lang-en-us/actions/inventory.js):
#
#   inventory_empty  → "{You} aren't carrying anything."
#   nothing_at_all   → "{You} aren't carrying anything at all."
#   hands_empty      → "{Your} hands are empty."
#   pockets_empty    → "{Your} pockets are empty."
#
# The contains_any below names the substrings that distinguish each variant.
# A new variant added by lang-en-us / stdlib that lacks all three keywords
# will fail this assertion on the run that draws it — that's the regression
# signal. A variant removal won't be detected by a single run, but over many
# CI runs the picker will stop drawing the removed key (silent drift, not a
# failure — note this in the philosophy doc).
#
# Rationale for repeated calls: one trial samples one variant. Ten trials
# at 4 variants ≈ very high probability of seeing at least 3 distinct
# variants per CI run, which gives the assertion meaningful exposure to
# the full set inside a single execution.

# The player starts at the Zoo Entrance with empty hands, so > inventory
# on turn 1 hits the empty branch deterministically (only the chosen
# variant text is non-deterministic, not whether the branch is taken).

> inventory
[OK: contains_any "carrying anything" "hands are empty" "pockets are empty"]

> inventory
[OK: contains_any "carrying anything" "hands are empty" "pockets are empty"]

> inventory
[OK: contains_any "carrying anything" "hands are empty" "pockets are empty"]

> inventory
[OK: contains_any "carrying anything" "hands are empty" "pockets are empty"]

> inventory
[OK: contains_any "carrying anything" "hands are empty" "pockets are empty"]

> inventory
[OK: contains_any "carrying anything" "hands are empty" "pockets are empty"]

> inventory
[OK: contains_any "carrying anything" "hands are empty" "pockets are empty"]

> inventory
[OK: contains_any "carrying anything" "hands are empty" "pockets are empty"]

> inventory
[OK: contains_any "carrying anything" "hands are empty" "pockets are empty"]

